# 基础词 Unit19
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit19核心词汇

{{abandon}}{{/əˈbændən}}{{v. 放弃；抛弃}}{{He abandoned his plan to study abroad due to financial difficulties.}}
{{abstract}}{{/ˈæbstrækt}}{{adj./n. 抽象的；摘要}}{{The concept of infinity is too abstract for young children.}}
{{absurd}}{{/əbˈsɜːd}}{{adj. 荒谬的；可笑的}}{{It is absurd to believe that the earth is flat.}}
{{academic}}{{/ˌækəˈdemɪk}}{{adj./n. 学术的；学者}}{{She published several academic papers on climate change.}}
{{accelerate}}{{/əkˈseləreɪt}}{{v. 加速；促进}}{{The government aims to accelerate economic growth.}}
{{accommodate}}{{/əˈkɒmədeɪt}}{{v. 容纳；提供住宿}}{{The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests.}}
{{accomplish}}{{/əˈkʌmplɪʃ}}{{v. 完成；实现}}{{He accomplished his goal of running a marathon.}}
{{accumulate}}{{/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt}}{{v. 积累；积聚}}{{Dust had accumulated on the shelves over the months.}}
{{accurate}}{{/ˈækjərət}}{{adj. 准确的；精确的}}{{The report provides an accurate description of the situation.}}
{{acknowledge}}{{/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ}}{{v. 承认；致谢}}{{He acknowledged his mistake and apologized publicly.}}
{{acquire}}{{/əˈkwaɪər}}{{v. 获得；学到}}{{She acquired a new skill through online courses.}}
{{adapt}}{{/əˈdæpt}}{{v. 适应；改编}}{{It is important to adapt to changing circumstances.}}
{{adequate}}{{/ˈædɪkwət}}{{adj. 足够的；适当的}}{{The supply of food is adequate for the refugees.}}
{{adjust}}{{/əˈdʒʌst}}{{v. 调整；适应}}{{You need to adjust the mirror before driving.}}
{{adopt}}{{/əˈdɒpt}}{{v. 采用；收养}}{{The company decided to adopt a new strategy.}}
{{advocate}}{{/ˈædvəkeɪt}}{{v./n. 提倡；倡导者}}{{Many scientists advocate for renewable energy sources.}}
{{affect}}{{/əˈfekt}}{{v. 影响；感动}}{{The new policy will affect millions of workers.}}
{{aggressive}}{{/əˈɡresɪv}}{{adj. 侵略性的；有进取心的}}{{The company adopted an aggressive marketing strategy.}}
{{allocate}}{{/ˈæləkeɪt}}{{v. 分配；拨出}}{{The government allocated funds for education.}}
{{ambiguous}}{{/æmˈbɪɡjuəs}}{{adj. 模棱两可的；含糊的}}{{The instructions were ambiguous and confusing.}}
{{amend}}{{/əˈmend}}{{v. 修改；改善}}{{The law was amended to include new provisions.}}
{{analogy}}{{/əˈnælədʒi}}{{n. 类比；类推}}{{He drew an analogy between the brain and a computer.}}
{{anticipate}}{{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt}}{{v. 预期；期望}}{{We anticipate a significant increase in demand.}}
{{apparent}}{{/əˈpærənt}}{{adj. 明显的；表面上的}}{{It was apparent that she was not telling the truth.}}
{{applicable}}{{/əˈplɪkəbl}}{{adj. 适用的；可应用的}}{{The rule is applicable to all employees.}}
{{appraise}}{{/əˈpreɪz}}{{v. 评估；鉴定}}{{Experts appraised the value of the painting.}}
{{appreciate}}{{/əˈpriːʃieɪt}}{{v. 感激；欣赏}}{{I really appreciate your help with this project.}}
{{approach}}{{/əˈprəʊtʃ}}{{v./n. 接近；方法}}{{We need to approach this problem from a different perspective.}}
{{appropriate}}{{/əˈprəʊpriət}}{{adj. 适当的；合适的}}{{Please wear appropriate clothing for the interview.}}
{{arbitrary}}{{/ˈɑːbɪtrəri}}{{adj. 任意的；武断的}}{{The decision seemed arbitrary and unfair.}}
{{arise}}{{/əˈraɪz}}{{v. 出现；产生}}{{New challenges may arise during the project.}}
{{articulate}}{{/ɑːˈtɪkjuleɪt}}{{adj./v. 善于表达的；清楚表达}}{{She is very articulate and persuasive in debates.}}
{{assert}}{{/əˈsɜːt}}{{v. 断言；主张；维护}}{{She asserted her right to speak at the meeting.}}
{{assess}}{{/əˈses}}{{v. 评估；评价}}{{Teachers assess students' progress through regular tests.}}
{{assign}}{{/əˈsaɪn}}{{v. 分配；指定}}{{The teacher assigned homework to the students.}}
{{assume}}{{/əˈsjuːm}}{{v. 假设；承担}}{{Let's assume that the project will be completed on time.}}
{{assure}}{{/əˈʃʊər}}{{v. 保证；使确信}}{{I assure you that the product is of high quality.}}
{{attach}}{{/əˈtætʃ}}{{v. 附上；重视}}{{Please attach your resume to the email.}}
{{attain}}{{/əˈteɪn}}{{v. 达到；获得}}{{She attained the highest score in the class.}}
{{attribute}}{{/əˈtrɪbjuːt}}{{v./n. 归因于；属性}}{{She attributed her success to hard work.}}
{{authentic}}{{/ɔːˈθentɪk}}{{adj. 真正的；真实的}}{{The restaurant serves authentic Italian food.}}
{{authorize}}{{/ˈɔːθəraɪz}}{{v. 授权；批准}}{{The manager authorized the purchase of new equipment.}}
{{automate}}{{/ˈɔːtəmeɪt}}{{v. 使自动化}}{{The factory automated its production line.}}
{{available}}{{/əˈveɪləbl}}{{adj. 可用的；有空的}}{{The manager is not available at the moment.}}
{{aware}}{{/əˈweər}}{{adj. 意识到的；知道的}}{{Are you aware of the risks involved in this project?}}
{{barrier}}{{/ˈbæriər}}{{n. 障碍；屏障}}{{Language can be a barrier to communication.}}
{{benefit}}{{/ˈbenɪfɪt}}{{n./v. 好处；受益}}{{Regular exercise has many health benefits.}}
{{bias}}{{/ˈbaɪəs}}{{n./v. 偏见；偏向}}{{The report was criticized for its political bias.}}
{{bond}}{{/bɒnd}}{{n./v. 纽带；联系；结合}}{{The mother and child share a strong emotional bond.}}
{{boom}}{{/buːm}}{{n./v. 繁荣；隆隆声}}{{The tech industry experienced a boom in the 2000s.}}
{{boost}}{{/buːst}}{{v./n. 促进；增加}}{{The new policy will boost the economy.}}
{{brief}}{{/briːf}}{{adj./n. 简短的；摘要}}{{He gave a brief summary of the report.}}
{{budget}}{{/ˈbʌdʒɪt}}{{n./v. 预算；编预算}}{{The government increased the education budget this year.}}
{{burden}}{{/ˈbɜːdn}}{{n./v. 负担；使负重}}{{The financial burden was too heavy for the family.}}
{{campaign}}{{/kæmˈpeɪn}}{{n./v. 运动；战役}}{{The marketing campaign was a huge success.}}
{{candidate}}{{/ˈkændɪdət}}{{n. 候选人；应试者}}{{There are five candidates for the position.}}
{{capacity}}{{/kəˈpæsəti}}{{n. 能力；容量；身份}}{{The stadium has a capacity of 50,000 spectators.}}
{{capture}}{{/ˈkæptʃər}}{{v./n. 捕获；夺取}}{{The photographer captured a beautiful sunset.}}
{{casual}}{{/ˈkæʒuəl}}{{adj. 随便的；偶然的}}{{He wore casual clothes to the party.}}
{{catastrophe}}{{/kəˈtæstrəfi}}{{n. 灾难；大祸}}{{The oil spill was an environmental catastrophe.}}
{{category}}{{/ˈkætəɡəri}}{{n. 种类；类别}}{{The books are arranged by category in the library.}}
{{cease}}{{/siːs}}{{v. 停止；终止}}{{The factory ceased production due to lack of raw materials.}}
{{challenge}}{{/ˈtʃælɪndʒ}}{{n./v. 挑战；质疑}}{{Learning a new language is always a challenge.}}
{{chronic}}{{/ˈkrɒnɪk}}{{adj. 慢性的；长期的}}{{He suffers from chronic back pain.}}
{{circumstance}}{{/ˈsɜːkəmstəns}}{{n. 环境；情况}}{{Under no circumstance should you give up.}}
{{cite}}{{/saɪt}}{{v. 引用；举例}}{{He cited several examples to support his argument.}}
{{claim}}{{/kleɪm}}{{v./n. 声称；索赔}}{{He claims to have seen a UFO.}}
{{clarify}}{{/ˈklærɪfaɪ}}{{v. 澄清；阐明}}{{Could you clarify what you mean by that statement?}}
{{collapse}}{{/kəˈlæps}}{{v./n. 倒塌；崩溃}}{{The building collapsed during the earthquake.}}
{{colleague}}{{/ˈkɒliːɡ}}{{n. 同事}}{{She gets along well with her colleagues at work.}}
{{combine}}{{/kəmˈbaɪn}}{{v. 结合；联合}}{{The company combined two departments to improve efficiency.}}
{{commit}}{{/kəˈmɪt}}{{v. 犯(罪)；承诺；投入}}{{He committed himself to finishing the project on time.}}
{{communicate}}{{/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt}}{{v. 交流；传达}}{{It is important to communicate effectively with your team.}}
{{community}}{{/kəˈmjuːnəti}}{{n. 社区；群体}}{{The local community organized a charity event.}}
{{compare}}{{/kəmˈpeər}}{{v. 比较；对比}}{{Compare the prices before making a purchase.}}
{{compel}}{{/kəmˈpel}}{{v. 迫使；强迫}}{{The evidence compelled him to change his mind.}}
{{compensate}}{{/ˈkɒmpenseɪt}}{{v. 补偿；赔偿}}{{The company compensated the workers for their overtime.}}
{{compete}}{{/kəmˈpiːt}}{{v. 竞争；比赛}}{{Several companies are competing for the contract.}}
{{competent}}{{/ˈkɒmpɪtənt}}{{adj. 有能力的；胜任的}}{{She is a competent manager with years of experience.}}
{{complain}}{{/kəmˈpleɪn}}{{v. 抱怨；投诉}}{{Customers complained about the poor service.}}
{{complex}}{{/ˈkɒmpleks}}{{adj./n. 复杂的；综合体}}{{The issue is more complex than it appears.}}
{{complicated}}{{/ˈkɒmplɪkeɪtɪd}}{{adj. 复杂的；难懂的}}{{The instructions were too complicated to follow.}}
{{component}}{{/kəmˈpəʊnənt}}{{n. 成分；部件}}{{Each component of the machine must be checked regularly.}}
{{compose}}{{/kəmˈpəʊz}}{{v. 组成；创作；使镇定}}{{The team is composed of experts from various fields.}}
{{comprehensive}}{{/ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv}}{{adj. 全面的；综合的}}{{The report provides a comprehensive analysis of the situation.}}
{{compromise}}{{/ˈkɒmprəmaɪz}}{{n./v. 妥协；折中}}{{Both sides reached a compromise after long negotiations.}}
{{conceive}}{{/kənˈsiːv}}{{v. 构想；怀孕；认为}}{{She conceived a plan to improve efficiency.}}
{{concentrate}}{{/ˈkɒnsntreɪt}}{{v. 集中；浓缩}}{{I need to concentrate on my studies without distractions.}}
{{concept}}{{/ˈkɒnsept}}{{n. 概念；观念}}{{The concept of freedom means different things to different people.}}
{{concern}}{{/kənˈsɜːn}}{{v./n. 关心；担忧；涉及}}{{Environmental pollution is a growing concern worldwide.}}
{{conclude}}{{/kənˈkluːd}}{{v. 结束；得出结论}}{{The study concluded that exercise improves mental health.}}
{{concrete}}{{/ˈkɒŋkriːt}}{{adj./n. 具体的；混凝土}}{{Please provide concrete evidence to support your claim.}}
{{condemn}}{{/kənˈdem}}{{v. 谴责；判刑}}{{The government condemned the terrorist attack.}}
{{conduct}}{{/kənˈdʌkt}}{{v./n. 进行；行为；指挥}}{{The scientist conducted an important experiment.}}
{{conference}}{{/ˈkɒnfərəns}}{{n. 会议；讨论会}}{{The international conference attracted scholars from around the world.}}
{{confess}}{{/kənˈfes}}{{v. 承认；坦白}}{{He confessed that he had lied about his qualifications.}}
{{confidence}}{{/ˈkɒnfɪdəns}}{{n. 信心；信任}}{{She spoke with confidence during the presentation.}}
{{confirm}}{{/kənˈfɜːm}}{{v. 确认；证实}}{{The hotel confirmed our reservation by email.}}
{{conflict}}{{/ˈkɒnflɪkt}}{{n./v. 冲突；矛盾}}{{The conflict between the two countries lasted for years.}}
{{confuse}}{{/kənˈfjuːz}}{{v. 使困惑；混淆}}{{The similar names often confuse people.}}
{{conscience}}{{/ˈkɒnʃəns}}{{n. 良心；道德心}}{{His conscience would not allow him to cheat.}}
{{conscious}}{{/ˈkɒnʃəs}}{{adj. 有意识的；自觉的}}{{She was conscious of the need to save money.}}
{{consensus}}{{/kənˈsensəs}}{{n. 共识；一致}}{{The committee reached a consensus on the new policy.}}
{{consequence}}{{/ˈkɒnsɪkwəns}}{{n. 结果；后果}}{{Climate change has serious consequences for the planet.}}
{{conservative}}{{/kənˈsɜːvətɪv}}{{adj./n. 保守的；保守派}}{{He holds conservative views on social issues.}}
{{considerable}}{{/kənˈsɪdərəbl}}{{adj. 相当大的；重要的}}{{The project requires a considerable amount of funding.}}
{{consist}}{{/kənˈsɪst}}{{v. 由…组成；在于}}{{The committee consists of ten members.}}
{{consistent}}{{/kənˈsɪstənt}}{{adj. 一致的；持续的}}{{Her performance has been consistent throughout the season.}}
{{constant}}{{/ˈkɒnstənt}}{{adj./n. 不变的；常数}}{{The machine operates at a constant speed.}}
{{constitute}}{{/ˈkɒnstɪtjuːt}}{{v. 构成；组成}}{{Women constitute more than half of the population.}}
{{construct}}{{/kənˈstrʌkt}}{{v. 建造；构造}}{{They plan to construct a new hospital in the area.}}
{{consult}}{{/kənˈsʌlt}}{{v. 咨询；查阅}}{{You should consult a doctor about your symptoms.}}
{{consume}}{{/kənˈsjuːm}}{{v. 消耗；消费；吃喝}}{{The car consumes a lot of fuel.}}
{{contact}}{{/ˈkɒntækt}}{{n./v. 接触；联系}}{{Please contact me if you have any questions.}}
{{contain}}{{/kənˈteɪn}}{{v. 包含；控制}}{{The box contains all the necessary documents.}}
{{contemporary}}{{/kənˈtemprəri}}{{adj./n. 当代的；同时代的人}}{{The museum has a fine collection of contemporary art.}}
{{content}}{{/ˈkɒntent}}{{n./adj. 内容；满足的}}{{She was content with her simple life.}}
{{contest}}{{/ˈkɒntest}}{{n./v. 竞赛；争辩}}{{She won first prize in the speech contest.}}
{{context}}{{/ˈkɒntekst}}{{n. 上下文；背景}}{{The meaning of the word depends on the context.}}
{{contradict}}{{/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt}}{{v. 反驳；与…矛盾}}{{The evidence contradicts his earlier statement.}}
{{contrary}}{{/ˈkɒntrəri}}{{adj./n. 相反的；对立面}}{{On the contrary, I think we should continue.}}
{{contrast}}{{/ˈkɒntrɑːst}}{{n./v. 对比；对照}}{{There is a sharp contrast between the rich and the poor.}}
{{contribute}}{{/kənˈtrɪbjuːt}}{{v. 贡献；捐献}}{{Everyone should contribute to the protection of the environment.}}
{{controversial}}{{/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃl}}{{adj. 有争议的}}{{The new law is highly controversial among citizens.}}
{{convenient}}{{/kənˈviːniənt}}{{adj. 方便的；便利的}}{{The location of the hotel is very convenient for tourists.}}
{{convention}}{{/kənˈvenʃn}}{{n. 大会；惯例；公约}}{{The annual convention will be held in Shanghai.}}
{{convince}}{{/kənˈvɪns}}{{v. 使确信；说服}}{{She convinced him to change his mind.}}
{{cooperate}}{{/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt}}{{v. 合作；配合}}{{The two companies agreed to cooperate on the project.}}
{{cope}}{{/kəʊp}}{{v. 应对；处理}}{{She learned to cope with stress through meditation.}}
{{core}}{{/kɔːr}}{{n./adj. 核心；核心的}}{{Innovation is the core of the company's strategy.}}
{{corporate}}{{/ˈkɔːpərət}}{{adj. 公司的；法人的}}{{The company announced a new corporate strategy.}}
{{correspond}}{{/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd}}{{v. 通信；相当于；符合}}{{The data does not correspond with the previous results.}}
{{crucial}}{{/ˈkruːʃl}}{{adj. 至关重要的；决定性的}}{{Education is crucial for the development of a country.}}
{{cultivate}}{{/ˈkʌltɪveɪt}}{{v. 培养；耕种}}{{Schools should cultivate students' creativity.}}
